-- LAYER 1, regulations 30 to 32: the timing of verification, insolvent bank customers, register discrepancies, ceasing transactions, trustees of debt issues.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE.  As in regulation 29, a duty is an engaged function (`... must ...`) and a checklist (`... has ...`); an exception worded "unless", "provided that" or
-- "does not apply" is an input of the engaged function; a gate or case worded "where", "when" or "if" that is not met answers JUST FALSE (ruling 2026-11-05, (b); fork F-when), a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING
-- (ruling 2026-11-05, (c)); a flat negative ("must not",
-- "does not apply", "is not required") answers JUST FALSE for the act it forbids or the duty it removes.

§ `Regulation 30 -- Timing of verification`

-- reg 30(8).  In this regulation, "insolvent bank customer" has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5): a pointer inside this part, taken as an input.
-- src:922 | (8) In this regulation, “insolvent bank customer” has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5).
@ref reg 30(8) (src:922-922)
GIVEN `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30(8) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insolvent bank customer” has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5)" (regulation 30ZA(5) answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by regulation 30ZA(5)

-- reg 30(1A).  This regulation does not apply to a credit institution in relation to an insolvent bank customer where regulation 30ZA applies.
-- src:909 | (1A) This regulation does not apply to a credit institution in relation to an insolvent bank customer where regulation 30ZA applies.
@ref reg 30(1A) (src:909-909)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `reg 30(8) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulation 30ZA applies to the credit institution in relation to the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30(1A) this regulation does not apply to the credit institution in relation to the insolvent bank customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem `credit institution` `the kinds of the relevant person` AND `reg 30(8) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `regulation 30ZA applies to the credit institution in relation to the customer` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem `credit institution` `the kinds of the relevant person` AND `reg 30(8) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`regulation 30ZA applies to the credit institution in relation to the customer`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where regulation 30ZA applies" is not met (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This regulation does not apply to a credit institution in relation to an insolvent bank customer ..."; the paragraph says nothing of a person who is not a credit institution, or of a customer who is not an insolvent bank customer (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")

-- reg 30(1).  Subject to paragraph (1A), this regulation applies when a relevant person is required to take any measures under regulation 27, 28 or 29.
