        IF `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `reg 28(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this regulation applies when a relevant person is required to take any measures under regulation 27, 28 or 29" (assumed 2026-11-05, fork F-when: "when" read as "where"; ruling (b): a "where" condition not met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): none of regulations 27, 28 and 29 has been answered as requiring measures, and not every one has been answered as not requiring them

-- reg 30(3).  Provided that the verification is completed as soon as practicable after contact is first established, the verification of the customer, any
