§ `Regulation 30ZA -- Insolvent bank customers`

-- reg 30ZA(5).  In this regulation "insolvency date" in respect of an insolvent bank means the date on which a bank insolvency order is made in relation to
-- the bank under section 94 (the order) of the Banking Act 2009.
-- src:936 | (5) In this regulation—
-- src:937 | “insolvency date” in respect of an insolvent bank means the date on which a bank insolvency order is made in relation to the bank under section 94 (the order) of the Banking Act 2009.
@ref reg 30ZA(5) (src:936-937)
GIVEN `the date on which a bank insolvency order is made in relation to the bank under section 94 of the Banking Act 2009` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 30ZA(5) the insolvency date in respect of the insolvent bank` MEANS
    JUST `the date on which a bank insolvency order is made in relation to the bank under section 94 of the Banking Act 2009`

-- src:938 | “insolvent bank” means either—
-- src:939 | a bank as defined in section 2 (interpretation: “bank”) of the Banking Act 2009 that has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of that Act; or
-- src:940 | a building society as defined in section 119 (interpretation) of the Building Societies Act 1986 that has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of the Banking Act 2009, as applied and modified by section 90C (application of bank insolvency and administration legislation to building societies) of the Building Societies Act 1986;
@ref reg 30ZA(5) (src:938-940)
GIVEN `the bank (as defined in section 2 of the Banking Act 2009) has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building society (as defined in section 119 of the Building Societies Act 1986) has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of the Banking Act 2009, as applied and modified by section 90C of the Building Societies Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(5) the institution is an insolvent bank` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the bank (as defined in section 2 of the Banking Act 2009) has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of that Act` OR `the building society (as defined in section 119 of the Building Societies Act 1986) has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of the Banking Act 2009, as applied and modified by section 90C of the Building Societies Act 1986` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insolvent bank” means either— a bank ... that has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of that Act; or a building society ... that has entered into the procedure in Part 2 of the Banking Act 2009"

-- reg 30ZA(5) "insolvent bank customer", the thirty days.  "Within the period of 30 days beginning with the insolvency date" is read so that the
-- insolvency date itself is the first day and the thirtieth day is the insolvency date plus 29 (Marginal readings, (d)).
-- src:941 | “insolvent bank customer” means any customer—
-- src:942 | which the credit institution is reasonably satisfied was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank; and
-- src:943 | with whom the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship within the period of 30 days beginning with the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank.
@ref reg 30ZA(5) (src:941-943)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 30ZA(5) the period of 30 days` MEANS 30

@ref reg 30ZA(5) (src:941-943)
GIVEN `the credit institution is reasonably satisfied that the customer was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer` IS A DATE
      `the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the credit institution is reasonably satisfied that the customer was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insolvent bank customer” means any customer— which the credit institution is reasonably satisfied was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank"
        IF (Day `the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer`) MINUS (Day `the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank`) AT LEAST 0 AND (Day `the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer`) MINUS (Day `the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank`) AT MOST (`reg 30ZA(5) the period of 30 days` MINUS 1) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with whom the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship within the period of 30 days beginning with the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank"

-- reg 30ZA(2).  Before permitting an insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1), the credit institution must
-- (a) identify the customer in accordance with regulation 28(2)(a); and (b) where applicable, identify a person purporting to act on the customer's behalf and
-- verify that such person is authorised so to act in accordance with regulation 28(10)(a) and (b).
