-- src:926 | (a) identify the customer in accordance with regulation 28(2)(a); and
-- src:927 | (b) where applicable, identify a person purporting to act on the customer’s behalf and verify that such person is authorised so to act in accordance with regulation 28(10)(a) and (b).
@ref reg 30ZA(2) (src:925-927)
GIVEN `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution is permitting the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(2) the credit institution must identify the customer, and any person acting for the customer, before permitting the account to be opened` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF NOT (`the person is a credit institution`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person is a credit institution" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF NOT (`the credit institution is permitting the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the credit institution is permitting the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 30ZA(2) (src:926-927)
GIVEN `it has identified the customer in accordance with regulation 28(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where applicable, it has identified a person purporting to act on the customer's behalf and verified that such person is authorised so to act in accordance with regulation 28(10)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(2) the credit institution has done what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has identified the customer in accordance with regulation 28(2)(a)` AND `where applicable, it has identified a person purporting to act on the customer's behalf and verified that such person is authorised so to act in accordance with regulation 28(10)(a) and (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the credit institution must— (a) identify the customer in accordance with regulation 28(2)(a); and (b) where applicable, identify a person purporting to act on the customer's behalf" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 30ZA(1).  Subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), a credit institution may permit an insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it before
