      `the person is a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution has permitted the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(3)(a) the credit institution must apply the other customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28 as soon as practicable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF NOT (`the person is a credit institution`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person is a credit institution" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF NOT (`the credit institution has permitted the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the credit institution has permitted the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 30ZA(3)(a) (src:929-929)
GIVEN `it has applied the other customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(3)(a) the credit institution has applied the other customer due diligence measures as soon as practicable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has applied the other customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` AND `it did so as soon as practicable` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "apply the other customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28 as soon as practicable" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 30ZA(3)(b).  SEAM S-3 (asking): regulation 33(1) (module mlr2) answers whether enhanced customer due diligence is required.
-- src:930 | (b) if it becomes apparent that any of the situations or cases set out in regulation 33(1) apply, carry out no further transactions from the insolvent bank customer’s account until it has completed the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, with the exception of regulation 28(11).
@ref reg 30ZA(3)(b) (src:930-930)
GIVEN `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution has permitted the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution has completed the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, with the exception of regulation 28(11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(3)(b) the credit institution may carry out further transactions from the insolvent bank customer's account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the credit institution has permitted the insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After permitting an insolvent bank customer to open an account and transact from it under paragraph (1)" (permission form of a prohibition, fork F-polarity: an unmet condition says nothing about whether the person may)
        IF `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the credit institution has completed the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, with the exception of regulation 28(11)`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "carry out no further transactions from the insolvent bank customer's account until it has completed the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28, with the exception of regulation 28(11)"
        IF `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): once the measures are completed the paragraph says nothing more; it grants no permission
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "if it becomes apparent that any of the situations or cases set out in regulation 33(1) apply"; regulation 33(1) has not answered that they do

DECLARE `reg 30ZA party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 30ZA the credit institution`

DECLARE `reg 30ZA act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 30ZA(3)(b) carry out a further transaction from the insolvent bank customer's account`

`reg 30ZA(3)(b) the prohibition on further transactions from the insolvent bank customer's account` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 30ZA the credit institution`
    SHANT `reg 30ZA(3)(b) carry out a further transaction from the insolvent bank customer's account`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 30ZA the credit institution` BECAUSE "the credit institution carried out a further transaction from the insolvent bank customer's account before completing the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28"

#TRACE `reg 30ZA(3)(b) the prohibition on further transactions from the insolvent bank customer's account` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 30ZA the credit institution` DOES `reg 30ZA(3)(b) carry out a further transaction from the insolvent bank customer's account` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 30ZA(3)(b) the prohibition on further transactions from the insolvent bank customer's account` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- reg 30ZA(4).  For the purposes of this regulation, a credit institution is to be treated as identifying an insolvent bank customer that is a body
-- corporate if the credit institution (a) obtains the information listed in regulation 28(3)(a); and (b) where the insolvent bank customer is not a company
-- which is listed on a regulated market (i) takes reasonable measures to determine the information listed in regulation 28(3)(b); and (ii) identifies the
-- beneficial owner where the customer is beneficially owned by another person.
-- src:931 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation, a credit institution is to be treated as identifying an insolvent bank customer that is a body corporate if the credit institution—
-- src:932 | (a) obtains the information listed in regulation 28(3)(a); and
-- src:933 | (b) where the insolvent bank customer is not a company which is listed on a regulated market—
-- src:934 | (i) takes reasonable measures to determine the information listed in regulation 28(3)(b); and
-- src:935 | (ii) identifies the beneficial owner where the customer is beneficially owned by another person.
@ref reg 30ZA(4) (src:931-935)
GIVEN `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the insolvent bank customer is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution obtains the information listed in regulation 28(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insolvent bank customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution takes reasonable measures to determine the information listed in regulation 28(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insolvent bank customer is beneficially owned by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the credit institution identifies the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30ZA(4) the credit institution is to be treated as identifying the insolvent bank customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a credit institution is to be treated as identifying an insolvent bank customer"
        IF NOT (`the insolvent bank customer is a body corporate`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an insolvent bank customer that is a body corporate"
        IF `the credit institution obtains the information listed in regulation 28(3)(a)` AND (`the insolvent bank customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market` OR (`the credit institution takes reasonable measures to determine the information listed in regulation 28(3)(b)` AND ((NOT (`the insolvent bank customer is beneficially owned by another person`)) OR `the credit institution identifies the beneficial owner`))) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be treated as identifying an insolvent bank customer that is a body corporate if the credit institution— (a) obtains the information listed in regulation 28(3)(a); and (b) where the insolvent bank customer is not a company which is listed on a regulated market— (i) takes reasonable measures ...; and (ii) identifies the beneficial owner where the customer is beneficially owned by another person" (Marginal readings, (a))

§ `Regulation 30A -- Requirement to report discrepancies in registers`

DECLARE `reg 30A(1) type of customer` IS ONE OF
    `reg 30A(1)(a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006`
    `reg 30A(1)(b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009`
    `reg 30A(1)(c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009`
    `reg 30A(1)(d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017`
    `reg 30A(1)(e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations`
    `reg 30A(1)(f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022`
    `reg 30A(1) a customer of another type`

-- reg 30A(1).  Subject to paragraph (8A), before establishing a business relationship with (a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the
-- Companies Act 2006; (b) an unregistered company ...; (c) a limited liability partnership ...; (d) an eligible Scottish partnership ...; (e) a trust which is
-- subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations, or (f) an overseas entity ..., a relevant person must collect an excerpt of the register which
-- contains full details of any information specified in paragraph (1A) held on the register at the relevant time before the business relationship is established,
-- or must establish from its inspection of the register that there is no such information held on the register at that time.
-- src:945 | (1) Subject to paragraph (8A), before establishing a business relationship with—
-- src:946 | (a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006 (information about people with significant control);
-- src:947 | (b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009;
-- src:948 | (c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009;
-- src:949 | (d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017, ...
-- src:950 | (e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations, or
-- src:951 | (f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022,
-- src:952 | a relevant person must collect an excerpt of the register which contains full details of any information specified in paragraph (1A) held on the register at the relevant time before the business relationship is established, or must establish from its inspection of the register that there is no such information held on the register at that time.
@ref reg 30A(1) (src:945-952)
GIVEN customerType IS A `reg 30A(1) type of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(1) the customer is of a type described in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER customerType
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 30A(1) a customer of another type` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before establishing a business relationship with (a) ... (f)"; the paragraph says nothing of a customer of another type

@ref reg 30A(1) (src:945-952)
GIVEN `reg 30A(1) the customer is of a type described in paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is establishing a business relationship with the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(1) the relevant person must collect an excerpt of the register or establish from its inspection that there is no such information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 30A(1) the customer is of a type described in paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before establishing a business relationship with (a) ... (f)"
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is establishing a business relationship with the customer`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before establishing a business relationship"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 30A(1) (src:945-952)
GIVEN `the relevant person collected an excerpt of the register which contains full details of any information specified in paragraph (1A) held on the register at the relevant time, or established from its inspection of the register that there is no such information held on the register at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so before the business relationship was established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 30A(8A) the credit institution may comply with the requirement in paragraph (1) after the establishment of a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(1) the relevant person has met the requirement of paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relevant person collected an excerpt of the register which contains full details of any information specified in paragraph (1A) held on the register at the relevant time, or established from its inspection of the register that there is no such information held on the register at that time` AND (`it did so before the business relationship was established` OR `reg 30A(8A) the credit institution may comply with the requirement in paragraph (1) after the establishment of a business relationship` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person must collect an excerpt of the register which contains full details of any information specified in paragraph (1A) ... before the business relationship is established, or must establish from its inspection of the register that there is no such information" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not met)

-- reg 30A(1A).  The information specified in this paragraph is (a) in relation to a firm of a type described in paragraphs (1)(a) to (e), information relating
-- to beneficial owners of the customer; and (b) in relation to an overseas entity of a type described in paragraph (1)(f), required information relating to
-- registrable beneficial owners specified under Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022.
-- src:953 | (1A) The information specified in this paragraph is as follows—
-- src:954 | (a) in relation to a firm of a type described in paragraphs (1)(a) to (e), information relating to beneficial owners of the customer; and
-- src:955 | (b) in relation to an overseas entity of a type described in paragraph (1)(f), required information relating to registrable beneficial owners specified under Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022.
@ref reg 30A(1A) (src:953-955)
GIVEN customerType IS A `reg 30A(1) type of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 30A(1A) the information specified for the type of customer` MEANS
    CONSIDER customerType
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST "information relating to beneficial owners of the customer"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009` THEN JUST "information relating to beneficial owners of the customer"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009` THEN JUST "information relating to beneficial owners of the customer"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017` THEN JUST "information relating to beneficial owners of the customer"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations` THEN JUST "information relating to beneficial owners of the customer"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN JUST "required information relating to registrable beneficial owners specified under Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1) a customer of another type` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1A) specifies information for the types described in paragraph (1) and for no other

-- reg 30A(8).  In this regulation, a "material discrepancy" is one described in Schedule 3AZA.
-- SEAM S-6 (asking): Schedule 3AZA (module mlr4) answers whether the discrepancy is a material discrepancy.
-- src:976 | (8) In this regulation, a “material discrepancy” is one described in Schedule 3AZA.
@ref reg 30A(8) (src:976-976)
GIVEN `sch 3AZA the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(8) the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sch 3AZA the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 3AZA the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “material discrepancy” is one described in Schedule 3AZA" (Schedule 3AZA answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 3AZA has not answered whether the discrepancy is one it describes

-- reg 30A(4).  The relevant person is not required under paragraph (2) or (2B) to report information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on
-- grounds of legal professional privilege in the High Court (or in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session).
-- src:967 | (4) The relevant person is not required under paragraph (2) or (2B) to report information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in the High Court (or in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session).
@ref reg 30A(4) (src:967-967)
GIVEN `the information is information which the relevant person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in the High Court, or in Scotland on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(4) the relevant person is required under paragraph (2) or (2B) to report the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is information which the relevant person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in the High Court, or in Scotland on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person is not required under paragraph (2) or (2B) to report information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph removes the requirement for privileged information and says nothing of other information (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)

-- reg 30A(2).  The relevant person must report to the person mentioned in paragraph (3) any material discrepancy the relevant person finds between information
-- relating to the beneficial ownership of the customer (a) which the relevant person collects under paragraph (1), and (b) which otherwise becomes available to
-- the relevant person in the course of carrying out its duties under these Regulations when establishing a business relationship with the customer.
-- src:956 | (2) The relevant person must report to the person mentioned in paragraph (3) any material discrepancy the relevant person finds between information relating to the beneficial ownership of the customer—
-- src:957 | (a) which the relevant person collects under paragraph (1), and
-- src:958 | (b) which otherwise becomes available to the relevant person in the course of carrying out its duties under these Regulations when establishing a business relationship with the customer.
@ref reg 30A(2) (src:956-958)
GIVEN `reg 30A(8) the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person finds the discrepancy between information which it collects under paragraph (1) and information which otherwise becomes available to it in the course of carrying out its duties under these Regulations when establishing a business relationship with the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is privileged: the relevant person would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(2) the relevant person must report the material discrepancy to the person mentioned in paragraph (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reg 30A(8) the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "reg 30A(8) the discrepancy is a material discrepancy" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF NOT (`the relevant person finds the discrepancy between information which it collects under paragraph (1) and information which otherwise becomes available to it in the course of carrying out its duties under these Regulations when establishing a business relationship with the customer`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant person finds the discrepancy between information which it collects under paragraph (1) and information which otherwise becomes available to it in the course of carrying out its duties under these Regulations when establishing a business relationship with the customer" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `the information is privileged: the relevant person would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person is not required under paragraph (2) or (2B) to report information which that person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in the High Court (or in Scotland, on the ground of confidentiality of communications in the Court of Session)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 30A(2) (src:956-958)
GIVEN `it has reported the material discrepancy to the person mentioned in paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(2) the relevant person has reported the material discrepancy to the person mentioned in paragraph (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has reported the material discrepancy to the person mentioned in paragraph (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The relevant person must report to the person mentioned in paragraph (3) any material discrepancy" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 30A(2A).  When taking measures to fulfil the duties to carry out customer due diligence and ongoing monitoring of a business relationship (including
