        IF NOT (`the relevant person is taking measures to fulfil the duties to carry out customer due diligence and ongoing monitoring of a business relationship under Part 3 of these Regulations after the business relationship has been established`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person is taking measures to fulfil the duties to carry out customer due diligence and ongoing monitoring of a business relationship under Part 3 of these Regulations after the business relationship has been established" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
