-- reg 30A(3).  A material discrepancy referred to in paragraphs (2) and (2B) must be reported (a) if it relates to a firm of a type described in paragraph (1)(a)
-- to (d), to the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006; (b) if it relates to a trust of a type described in paragraph (1)(e), to the
-- Commissioners; (c) if it relates to an overseas entity of a type described in paragraph (1)(f), to the registrar of companies for England and Wales.
DECLARE `reg 30A(3) person to whom a material discrepancy is reported` IS ONE OF
    `reg 30A(3)(a) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    `reg 30A(3)(b) the Commissioners`
    `reg 30A(3)(c) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`

-- src:963 | (3) A material discrepancy referred to in paragraphs (2) and (2B) must be reported—
-- src:964 | (a) if it relates to a firm of a type described in paragraph (1)(a) to (d), to the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006;
-- src:965 | (b) if it relates to a trust of a type described in paragraph (1)(e), to the Commissioners;
-- src:966 | (c) if it relates to an overseas entity of a type described in paragraph (1)(f), to the registrar of companies for England and Wales.
@ref reg 30A(3) (src:963-966)
GIVEN customerType IS A `reg 30A(1) type of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 30A(3) person to whom a material discrepancy is reported`
`reg 30A(3) the person to whom the material discrepancy must be reported` MEANS
    CONSIDER customerType
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(a) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(a) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(a) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(a) the registrar referred to in section 1060(3) of the Companies Act 2006`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(b) the Commissioners`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN JUST `reg 30A(3)(c) the registrar of companies for England and Wales`
    WHEN `reg 30A(1) a customer of another type` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (3) names the person to whom a discrepancy is reported for the types described in paragraph (1) and for no other

-- reg 30A(5).  The person to whom a material discrepancy is reported must take such action as that person considers appropriate to investigate and, if necessary,
-- resolve the discrepancy in a timely manner.
-- src:968 | (5) The person to whom a material discrepancy is reported must take such action as that person considers appropriate to investigate and, if necessary, resolve the discrepancy in a timely manner.
@ref reg 30A(5) (src:968-968)
GIVEN `it has taken such action as it considers appropriate to investigate and, if necessary, resolve the discrepancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has done so in a timely manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(5) the person to whom the material discrepancy is reported has taken the action that paragraph (5) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken such action as it considers appropriate to investigate and, if necessary, resolve the discrepancy` AND `it has done so in a timely manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person to whom a material discrepancy is reported must take such action as that person considers appropriate to investigate and, if necessary, resolve the discrepancy in a timely manner" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 30A(6).  A discrepancy which is reported to the registrar under paragraph (3) is material excluded from public inspection for the purposes of (a) section
-- 1087 of the Companies Act 2006 (material not available for public inspection), including for the purposes of that section as applied (i) to unregistered
-- companies by paragraph 20 of Schedule 1 to the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009; (ii) to limited liability partnerships by regulation 66 of the Limited
-- Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009; and (iii) to eligible Scottish partnerships by regulation 61 of the Scottish
-- Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017; and (b) section 22 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022
-- (material unavailable for inspection).
-- src:969 | (6) A discrepancy which is reported to the registrar under paragraph (3) is material excluded from public inspection for the purposes of—
-- src:970 | (a) section 1087 of the Companies Act 2006 (material not available for public inspection), including for the purposes of that section as applied—
-- src:971 | (i) to unregistered companies by paragraph 20 of Schedule 1 to the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009;
-- src:972 | (ii) to limited liability partnerships by regulation 66 of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009; and
-- src:973 | (iii) to eligible Scottish partnerships by regulation 61 of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017; and
-- src:974 | (b) section 22 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 (material unavailable for inspection).
@ref reg 30A(6) (src:969-974)
GIVEN `the discrepancy is reported to the registrar under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(6) the discrepancy is material excluded from public inspection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the discrepancy is reported to the registrar under paragraph (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A discrepancy which is reported to the registrar under paragraph (3)"; the paragraph says nothing of a discrepancy reported to the Commissioners

@ref reg 30A(6) (src:969-974)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 30A(6) the provisions for the purposes of which the discrepancy is excluded from public inspection` MEANS
    LIST "section 1087 of the Companies Act 2006 (material not available for public inspection)", "section 1087 as applied to unregistered companies by paragraph 20 of Schedule 1 to the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009", "section 1087 as applied to limited liability partnerships by regulation 66 of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009", "section 1087 as applied to eligible Scottish partnerships by regulation 61 of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017", "section 22 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 (material unavailable for inspection)"

-- reg 30A(8A).  In relation to an insolvent bank customer of a type described in any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (f) of paragraph (1), a credit institution may
-- comply with the requirement in paragraph (1) after the establishment of a business relationship with that customer.
-- src:977 | (8A) In relation to an insolvent bank customer of a type described in any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (f) of paragraph (1), a credit institution may comply with the requirement in paragraph (1) after the establishment of a business relationship with that customer.
@ref reg 30A(8A) (src:977-977)
GIVEN `the kinds of the relevant person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `reg 30A(8B) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 30A(1) the customer is of a type described in paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(8A) the credit institution may comply with the requirement in paragraph (1) after the establishment of a business relationship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem `credit institution` `the kinds of the relevant person` AND `reg 30A(8B) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `reg 30A(1) the customer is of a type described in paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to an insolvent bank customer of a type described in any of sub-paragraphs (a) to (f) of paragraph (1), a credit institution may comply ... after the establishment"; the paragraph says nothing of another case

-- reg 30A(8B).  In this regulation, "insolvent bank customer" has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5): a pointer inside this part, taken as an input.
-- src:978 | (8B) In this regulation, “insolvent bank customer” has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5).
@ref reg 30A(8B) (src:978-978)
GIVEN `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 30A(8B) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insolvent bank customer” has the meaning given in regulation 30ZA(5)" (regulation 30ZA(5) answers no)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by regulation 30ZA(5)

-- reg 30A(9).  In this regulation "the register" means (a) in relation to a customer of the type described in paragraph (1)(a), the register within the meaning of
-- section 1080(2) of the Companies Act 2006; (b) in relation to a customer which is a firm of a type described in paragraph (1)(b) to (d), the records of
-- information mentioned in section 1080(1)(a) of the Companies Act 2006 relating to such firm; (c) in relation to a customer which is an overseas entity of a type
-- described in paragraph (1)(f), the register referred to in section 3(1) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022.
-- src:979 | (9) In this regulation “the register” means—
-- src:980 | (a) in relation to a customer which is of the type described in paragraph (1)(a), the register within the meaning of section 1080(2) of the Companies Act 2006;
-- src:981 | (b) in relation to a customer which is a firm of a type described in paragraph (1)(b) to (d), the records of information mentioned in section 1080(1)(a) of the Companies Act 2006 relating to such firm;
-- src:982 | (c) in relation to a customer which is an overseas entity of a type described in paragraph (1)(f), the register referred to in section 3(1) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022.
@ref reg 30A(9) (src:979-982)
GIVEN customerType IS A `reg 30A(1) type of customer`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 30A(9) the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER customerType
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(a) a company which is subject to the requirements of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST "the register within the meaning of section 1080(2) of the Companies Act 2006"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(b) an unregistered company which is subject to the requirements of the Unregistered Companies Regulations 2009` THEN JUST "the records of information mentioned in section 1080(1)(a) of the Companies Act 2006 relating to such firm"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(c) a limited liability partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Limited Liability Partnerships (Application of Companies Act 2006) Regulations 2009` THEN JUST "the records of information mentioned in section 1080(1)(a) of the Companies Act 2006 relating to such firm"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(d) an eligible Scottish partnership which is subject to the requirements of the Scottish Partnerships (Register of People with Significant Control) Regulations 2017` THEN JUST "the records of information mentioned in section 1080(1)(a) of the Companies Act 2006 relating to such firm"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(e) a trust which is subject to registration under Part 5 of these Regulations` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (9) gives "the register" for customers of the types in paragraph (1)(a) to (d) and (f), and none for a trust of the type in paragraph (1)(e)
    WHEN `reg 30A(1)(f) an overseas entity which is subject to registration under Part 1 of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN JUST "the register referred to in section 3(1) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022"
    WHEN `reg 30A(1) a customer of another type` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (9) gives "the register" for the types described in paragraph (1) and for no other

§ `Regulation 31 -- Requirement to cease transactions etc`

-- reg 31(2).  Paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent money deposited in an account being repaid to the person who deposited it, provided that, in any case where a
-- disclosure is required by the legislation referred in paragraph (1)(d), the relevant person has (a) consent (within the meaning of section 21ZA of the Terrorism
-- Act 2000 (arrangements with prior consent)) to the transaction, or (b) the appropriate consent (within the meaning of section 335 of the Proceeds of Crime
-- Act 2002 (appropriate consent)) to the transaction.
-- src:991 | (2) Paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent money deposited in an account being repaid to the person who deposited it, provided that, in any case where a disclosure is required by the legislation referred in paragraph (1)(d), the relevant person has—
-- src:992 | (a) consent (within the meaning of section 21ZA of the Terrorism Act 2000 (arrangements with prior consent)) to the transaction, or
-- src:993 | (b) the appropriate consent (within the meaning of section 335 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (appropriate consent)) to the transaction.
@ref reg 31(2) (src:991-993)
GIVEN `the money deposited in an account is being repaid to the person who deposited it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disclosure is required by the legislation referred to in paragraph (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has consent (within the meaning of section 21ZA of the Terrorism Act 2000) to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has the appropriate consent (within the meaning of section 335 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002) to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the money deposited in an account is being repaid to the person who deposited it`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not prevent money deposited in an account being repaid to the person who deposited it"
        IF NOT (`a disclosure is required by the legislation referred to in paragraph (1)(d)`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the relevant person has consent (within the meaning of section 21ZA of the Terrorism Act 2000) to the transaction` OR `the relevant person has the appropriate consent (within the meaning of section 335 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002) to the transaction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that, in any case where a disclosure is required by the legislation referred in paragraph (1)(d), the relevant person has— (a) consent ... to the transaction, or (b) the appropriate consent ... to the transaction"

-- reg 31(3).  Paragraph (1) does not apply where an independent legal professional or other professional adviser is in the course of ascertaining the legal position
-- for a client or performing the task of defending or representing that client in, or concerning, legal proceedings, including giving advice on the institution or
-- avoidance of proceedings.
-- src:994 | (3) Paragraph (1) does not apply where an independent legal professional or other professional adviser is in the course of ascertaining the legal position for a client or performing the task of defending or representing that client in, or concerning, legal proceedings, including giving advice on the institution or avoidance of proceedings.
@ref reg 31(3) (src:994-994)
GIVEN `the person is an independent legal professional or other professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is in the course of ascertaining the legal position for a client or performing the task of defending or representing that client in, or concerning, legal proceedings, including giving advice on the institution or avoidance of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an independent legal professional or other professional adviser` AND `that person is in the course of ascertaining the legal position for a client or performing the task of defending or representing that client in, or concerning, legal proceedings, including giving advice on the institution or avoidance of proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply where an independent legal professional or other professional adviser is in the course of ..."; the paragraph says nothing of another case (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)

-- reg 31(4).  In paragraph (3), "other professional adviser" means an auditor, external accountant or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is
-- established for any such persons and which makes provision for (a) testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a
-- condition for such admission; and (b) imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for
-- non-compliance with those standards.
-- src:995 | (4) In paragraph (3), “other professional adviser” means an auditor, external accountant or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for any such persons and which makes provision for—
-- src:996 | (a) testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission; and
-- src:997 | (b) imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards.
@ref reg 31(4) (src:995-997)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor, external accountant or tax adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a professional body which is established for any such persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(4) the person is an other professional adviser` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an auditor, external accountant or tax adviser` AND `the person is a member of a professional body which is established for any such persons` AND `that body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission` AND `that body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“other professional adviser” means an auditor, external accountant or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for any such persons and which makes provision for— (a) ...; and (b) ..."

-- reg 31(5).  Paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply where an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company,
-- provided that (a) the insolvency practitioner has taken all reasonable steps to satisfy the requirements set out in regulation 28(2) and (10), and (b) the
-- resignation of the insolvency practitioner would be prejudicial to the interests of the creditors of the company.
-- src:998 | (5) Paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply where an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company, provided that—
-- src:999 | (a) the insolvency practitioner has taken all reasonable steps to satisfy the requirements set out in regulation 28(2) and (10), and
-- src:1000 | (b) the resignation of the insolvency practitioner would be prejudicial to the interests of the creditors of the company.
@ref reg 31(5) (src:998-1000)
GIVEN `an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insolvency practitioner has taken all reasonable steps to satisfy the requirements set out in regulation 28(2) and (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resignation of the insolvency practitioner would be prejudicial to the interests of the creditors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply where an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company" (Ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met)
        IF `the insolvency practitioner has taken all reasonable steps to satisfy the requirements set out in regulation 28(2) and (10)` AND `the resignation of the insolvency practitioner would be prejudicial to the interests of the creditors of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply where an insolvency practitioner has been appointed ..., provided that (a) the insolvency practitioner has taken all reasonable steps to satisfy the requirements set out in regulation 28(2) and (10), and (b) the resignation of the insolvency practitioner would be prejudicial to the interests of the creditors of the company"

-- reg 31(1)(a).  Where, in relation to any customer, a relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28, that person
-- must not carry out any transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer.
-- src:984 | (1) Where, in relation to any customer, a relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28, that person—
-- src:985 | (a) must not carry out any transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer;
@ref reg 31(1)(a) (src:984-985)
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(a) the relevant person may carry out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, in relation to any customer, a relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28" (this function asks the permission form, "may", of a prohibition: an unmet "where" leaves the question whether the person may carry out the transaction to the rest of the Regulations, so it answers NOTHING, not JUST TRUE; fork F-polarity)
        IF `reg 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1), and the text then says nothing about it
        IF `reg 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person— (a) must not carry out any transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer"

-- reg 31(1)(b).  ... that person must not establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account.
-- src:986 | (b) must not establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account;
@ref reg 31(1)(b) (src:986-986)
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(b) the relevant person may establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, in relation to any customer, a relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28" (this function asks the permission form, "may", of a prohibition: an unmet "where" leaves the question whether the person may carry out the transaction to the rest of the Regulations, so it answers NOTHING, not JUST TRUE; fork F-polarity)
        IF `reg 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1), and the text then says nothing about it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person— (b) must not establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account"

DECLARE `reg 31 party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 31 the relevant person`

DECLARE `reg 31 act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 31(1)(a) carry out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer`
    `reg 31(1)(b) establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account`

`reg 31(1)(a) the prohibition on transactions through a bank account` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 31 the relevant person`
    SHANT `reg 31(1)(a) carry out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 31 the relevant person` BECAUSE "the relevant person carried out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer while unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28"

`reg 31(1)(b) the prohibition on establishing a business relationship or carrying out a transaction otherwise than through a bank account` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 31 the relevant person`
    SHANT `reg 31(1)(b) establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 31 the relevant person` BECAUSE "the relevant person established a business relationship or carried out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account while unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28"

#TRACE `reg 31(1)(a) the prohibition on transactions through a bank account` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 31 the relevant person` DOES `reg 31(1)(a) carry out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 31(1)(a) the prohibition on transactions through a bank account` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

#TRACE `reg 31(1)(b) the prohibition on establishing a business relationship or carrying out a transaction otherwise than through a bank account` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 31 the relevant person` DOES `reg 31(1)(b) establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 31(1)(b) the prohibition on establishing a business relationship or carrying out a transaction otherwise than through a bank account` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- reg 31(1)(c).  ... that person must terminate any existing business relationship with the customer.
-- src:987 | (c) must terminate any existing business relationship with the customer;
@ref reg 31(1)(c) (src:987-987)
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(c) the relevant person must terminate any existing business relationship with the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
        IF `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply where an insolvency practitioner has been appointed by the court as administrator or liquidator of a company"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 31(1)(c) (src:987-987)
GIVEN `it has terminated the existing business relationship with the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(c) the relevant person has terminated the existing business relationship with the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has terminated the existing business relationship with the customer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person— (c) must terminate any existing business relationship with the customer" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 31(1)(d).  ... that person must consider whether the relevant person is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by (i) Part 3 of the
-- Terrorism Act 2000; or (ii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
-- src:988 | (d) must consider whether the relevant person is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by—
-- src:989 | (i) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ; or
-- src:990 | (ii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 .
@ref reg 31(1)(d) (src:988-990)
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(d) the relevant person must consider whether it is required to make a disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; "when", "upon", "whenever" read as "where", fork F-when)
        IF `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply where an independent legal professional or other professional adviser is in the course of ascertaining the legal position for a client or performing the task of defending or representing that client in, or concerning, legal proceedings"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 31(1)(d) (src:988-990)
GIVEN `it has considered whether it is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has considered whether it is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 31(1)(d) the relevant person has considered whether it is required to make a disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has considered whether it is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000` AND `it has considered whether it is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person— (d) must consider whether the relevant person is required to make a disclosure (or to make further disclosure) by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

§ `Regulation 32 -- Exception for trustees of debt issues`

-- reg 32(2).  The specified instruments and securities are (a) instruments which fall within article 77 or 77A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000
-- (Regulated Activities) Order 2001; and (b) securities which fall within article 78 of that Order.
-- src:1006 | (2) The specified instruments and securities are—
-- src:1007 | (a) instruments which fall within article 77 or 77A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 ; and
-- src:1008 | (b) securities which fall within article 78 of that Order .
@ref reg 32(2) (src:1006-1008)
GIVEN `the instruments fall within article 77 or 77A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities fall within article 78 of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instruments fall within article 77 or 77A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` OR `the securities fall within article 78 of that Order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The specified instruments and securities are— (a) instruments which fall within article 77 or 77A ...; and (b) securities which fall within article 78 of that Order"

-- reg 32(1).  A relevant person (a) who is appointed by the issuer of instruments or securities specified in paragraph (2) as trustee of an issue of such
-- instruments or securities; or (b) whose customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities, is not required to apply the customer due diligence
-- measure referred to in regulation 28(3) and (4) in respect of the holders of such instruments or securities.
-- src:1002 | (1) A relevant person—
-- src:1003 | (a) who is appointed by the issuer of instruments or securities specified in paragraph (2) as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities; or
-- src:1004 | (b) whose customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities,
-- src:1005 | is not required to apply the customer due diligence measure referred to in regulation 28(3) and (4) in respect of the holders of such instruments or securities.
@ref reg 32(1) (src:1002-1005)
GIVEN `the relevant person is appointed by the issuer of the instruments or securities as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person's customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 32(1) the relevant person is required to apply the customer due diligence measure referred to in regulation 28(3) and (4) in respect of the holders of the instruments or securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the relevant person is appointed by the issuer of the instruments or securities as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` OR `the relevant person's customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities`) AND `reg 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to apply the customer due diligence measure referred to in regulation 28(3) and (4) in respect of the holders of such instruments or securities"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph removes the requirement for the relevant persons it describes and says nothing of others (exception polarity, fork F-polarity: the function asks the question the exception answers no to, so an unmet condition leaves that question to the rest of the Regulations)
